Notebook[{
Cell["KPZ at LO: couplings that are functions of p^2", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"b1d2559f-e0bf-4b72-acd5-7aa97b72f2ac"],

Cell["\<\
The second pipeline of the library (design/LOPIPELINE.md). The Gamma2 \
couplings of KPZ become functions of the momentum: Gamma^(1,1) = i w + nu p^2 \
f_nu(p^2), Gamma^(0,2) = -2 D f_D(p^2), with f_nu(0) = f_D(0) = 1, the vertex \
lambda constant. The library derives the flow of each function at generic p \
(one loop, two pole families: Delta at q and at Q = p + q), the anomalous \
dimensions from f(0) = 1, the dimensionless form at fixed p/k, and writes a \
Python module for BMWflow. The exact comparison with BMWflow's notes \
(LO_flow_equations.tex, kpz_notation.tex) is the benchmark benchmarks/KPZLO; \
this notebook shows the workflow and checks f = 1 against Canet's Eq. (20).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2b8c8df3-42f0-4785-82e3-3640d8d9fe93"],

Cell["Get[\"~/Physics/Sources/FRGscalarMSR/FRGscalarMSR.wl\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a3cd647b-a063-43f1-a42f-2ee8f569ac4d"],

Cell["1. Ansatz with functions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d60a73f9-05fe-435b-9b0c-34c65f737fc0"],

Cell["\<\
fn[f, X] in the density is f(-Laplacian) acting on X: it multiplies the term \
by f(p^2), p the momentum of X's leg. \"Functions\" -> {f -> reference} \
states f(0) = 1 and names the k-dependent amplitude; the ansatz infers \
\"Pipeline\" -> \"LO\" from the fn. The symmetries take the same tags as in \
DE but no truncation orders: the Galilean Ward identity protects the 1 of i \
w, the shift symmetry h -> h + c makes the p^0 order of Gamma^(1,1) vanish.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4b8d63ed-1f94-41f4-b020-4dbace078f82"],

Cell["\<\
theory = DefineTheory[\"Scalars\" -> {h}, \"Dimension\" -> Dim];
ansatz = DefineAnsatz[theory,
  \"Density\" -> hbar (dt[h] - nuk fn[fnu, lap[h]] - lamk/2 grad[h].grad[h]) \
- Dk hbar fn[fD, hbar],
  \"Couplings\" -> {nuk, lamk, Dk}, \"Functions\" -> {fD -> Dk, fnu -> nuk}];\
\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"23290f30-a380-4583-9ba6-00389ff58f65"],

Cell["\<\
symmetries = DeclareSymmetries[ansatz,
  Protected[{hbar, h}, \"Frequency\" -> 1, \"Momentum\" -> 0, \"Reason\" -> \
\"Galilean Ward identity\"],
  Protected[{h, hbar}, \"Frequency\" -> 0, \"Momentum\" -> 0, \"Reason\" -> \
\"h -> h + c (shift symmetry)\"],
  NonRenormalised[lamk, \"Reason\" -> \"Galilean invariance\"]];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ff430506-ea22-4d64-bb59-711a34e336ca"],

Cell["2. Vertices, regulator, propagator, loops", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"94c70266-98ea-4813-92f6-80528cc39ec2"],

Cell["\<\
The same stages as in DE. The propagator atoms now contain fnu[s] and fD[s]; \
the regulator shapes are functions of q^2/k^2.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0bb49eb0-9fc3-48e1-bc78-79e2c63449d3"],

Cell["\<\
vertices = BuildVertices[ansatz];
regulator = DefineRegulator[ansatz, {hbar, h} -> nuk q^2 rn[q^2/k^2], {hbar, \
hbar} -> -2 Dk rd[q^2/k^2], \"Shapes\" -> {rn, rd}];
prop = BuildPropagator[vertices, regulator];
loops = BuildLoopIntegrands[vertices, prop, regulator];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"467f71ad-ae5e-4512-b845-fbf70e386a27"],

Cell["3. Flows at generic p", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5de1a5ca-d968-4f49-9363-a5bab530d889"],

Cell["\<\
BuildLOEquations replaces Projection ... Assemble. For each function it takes \
the loop at external momentum p and zero external frequency, integrates the \
loop frequency by residues at the poles of both families, and divides by the \
ansatz prefactor (nuk p^2 for fnu, -2 Dk for fD: P2Divided records the p^2). \
It checks that the entries outside the ansatz vanish at every p, the Ward \
identity, that the p^0 order of the fnu row vanishes, and builds the eta rows \
as the exact p -> 0 limit. The integrand is explicit in p, q, CosTheta = \
cos(p, q), f at q^2 and at Q^2 = p^2 + q^2 + 2 p q CosTheta, the shapes and \
dsCoupling.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"70056a73-3405-46a0-b87a-e11e0d4b18f2"],

Cell["\<\
equations = BuildLOEquations[loops, symmetries];
ShowLOEquation[equations, fD]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b12273b2-1f75-4388-9fc8-7a8d960cde98"],

Cell["oracle = RunOracle[equations, \"ZeroFlows\" -> True];", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"6847aa04-8dcb-4e1f-916c-773253935c08"],

Cell["4. Dimensionless flows", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"aad15057-21af-4244-91e0-7a442bd74a7d"],

Cell["\<\
F_k(p^2) = f(p^2/k^2), ap = p/k, aq = q/k. At fixed ap each function flows as \
d_s f = eta f + 2 ap^2 f'(ap^2) + Loop (integrated with Measure[\"Loop\"] \
over aq and theta). f(0) = 1 fixes the etas: (1 + <EtaMatrix>) eta = \
-<EtaVector>, with <.> = Integral daq Measure[\"Eta\"]. The constant coupling \
alamk = lamk Dk^(1/2) nuk^(-3/2) k^(d/2-1) has only a linear part.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"50771220-ad5a-46b2-af0b-e35413724385"],

Cell["\<\
dims = DeriveDimensions[ansatz, \"References\" -> {nuk -> \"nu\", Dk -> \
\"D\"}];
adim = AdimensionalEquations[equations, dims];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"27c0cdfe-64bb-4b0e-b1ed-744bfc6d19db"],

Cell["Thread[adim[\"Functions\"] -> adim[\"Linear\"]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a5d032d7-91e5-4b79-83f9-41ccf961bcc4"],

Cell["\<\
{adim[\"Etas\"], adim[\"Couplings\"] -> adim[\"BetaL\"], \
adim[\"Measure\"][\"Eta\"]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ef3be5ab-2a10-44e5-957c-0469b8bde481"],

Cell["Short[adim[\"Loop\"], 6]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3bf3f9c3-61d1-442a-bc40-62f38485f40c"],

Cell["5. Check: f = 1 gives Canet's Eq. (20)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"22771a7c-24be-415c-b064-a78e3aa94ff9"],

Cell["\<\
At f_D = f_nu = 1 the eta system is the one of the DE KPZ flow (KPZ.nb). With \
the Litim cutoff r(y) = 1/y - 1 for y < 1 in both sectors, the aq integral is \
elementary (y = aq^2). Measure[\"Eta\"] = v_d aq^(d-1) and Canet's g = v_d \
alamk^2, so v_d drops out with alamk^2 = g/v_d: set the v_d of the measure to \
1 and alamk^2 = g. The difference with Canet's d_s g/g is exactly 0 at every \
d.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a2e0cc27-0f51-4c0e-a842-fc54d74d0e36"],

Cell["\<\
litim = {fD -> Function[x, 1], fnu -> Function[x, 1], rn -> Function[y, 1/y - \
1], rd -> Function[y, 1/y - 1]};
litimAvg[f_] := Module[{e = Expand[Together[(f /. litim /. aq -> Sqrt[y] /. \
alamk -> Sqrt[g] /. Dim -> d)] y^(d/2 - 1)/2], terms},
  terms = If[Head[e] === Plus, List @@ e, {e}];
  Total[(# /. y -> 1)/(Exponent[#, y] + 1) & /@ terms]];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"1a5de54a-10ab-4f7f-ac87-5be4a4f3f67d"],

Cell["\<\
etas = Thread[adim[\"Etas\"] -> LinearSolve[IdentityMatrix[2] + Map[litimAvg, \
adim[\"EtaMatrix\"], {2}], -(litimAvg /@ adim[\"EtaVector\"])]];
bracket = Together[2 First[adim[\"BetaL\"]]/alamk /. etas /. Dim -> d]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8a8eff40-fd7b-415f-8ded-2da13f6cbc94"],

Cell["\<\
canet = (2 d^6 + 4 d^5 - d^4 (7 g + 8) - 2 d^3 (3 g + 8) + d^2 g (3 g + 20) - \
d (g - 8) g - 2 g^2)/
   (2 d^5 + 8 d^4 + d^3 (8 - 3 g) - 2 d^2 g + d g (g + 8) - g^2);
Together[bracket - canet]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5105802c-cdbe-4791-a1f9-374f57d5c221"],

Cell["6. The BMWflow module", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6040ed58-0a14-48df-8321-df79fd445ec2"],

Cell["\<\
ExportPython writes the module of the contract docs/handoff/BMWflow_LO.md: \
FUNCTIONS, ETAS, COUPLINGS, P2_DIVIDED and the functions linear, loop, \
eta_matrix, eta_vector, beta. The loop measure is not in the kernels (the \
adapter applies it); primes on f are d/d|momentum|. \"Model\" -> \"KPZ\" \
picks the row of PythonModelTable that maps alamk to BMWflow's g = alamk^2.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c0f62262-be73-4b54-aae1-b7c518db78e5"],

Cell["\<\
ExportPython[adim, \"Model\" -> \"KPZ\", \"File\" -> \
FileNameJoin[{$TemporaryDirectory, \"KPZLO\", \"KPZ_LO.py\"}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"01eacb58-af72-4105-a7c5-6a25dc8ae893"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"14.3 for Linux x86 (64-bit) (July 8, 2025)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"c6daf2f9-7a8d-42e7-81d6-335a272a6867"
]
